error[ffi_const_field]: `fixedbugs-2388-const-in-an-element.h` declares `Outer`'s member `k` as `const`, inside an element of one of `Outer`'s array members, so C still refuses to assign any `Outer` — and this line is that assignment
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2388-a-const-member-in-an-array-s-element-received-is-told.hero:24:11
     |
  24 |     got = fixedbugs_2388_outer_make()  #~ ffi_const_field
     |           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: C11 counts a `const` member inside an array's element as it counts one at the top (§6.3.2.1p1), though clang assigns it without a word: take one FROM the library through a pointer a function the group declares returns, rather than build it or receive it by value here
